# component-architecture

The documentation system implements a domain-specific component architecture focused on organizing CMS technical content:

## Core Organization Components
- Hierarchical content structure with specialized sections
- Domain-specific tag reference categorization
- Advanced tutorial content nesting
- Asset management subsystem

## Documentation Categories (Importance: 85)
Core documentation components organized into distinct business domains:
- Getting Started
- Concepts 
- Tags Reference
- Tutorials
- Tips & Tricks
- Add-Ons

## Specialized Tag Components (Importance: 90)
Domain-specific tag categorization system:
- Core tags implementation
- Sub-Templates framework
- Template Inheritance system
- Custom Routes engine
- Extended Entities model

## Tutorial Component System (Importance: 75)
Multi-level nested architecture for complex documentation:
- Code implementation sections
- Implementation guidelines
- Views documentation
- User management docs
- Controller documentation

## Asset Management (Importance: 65)
Documentation asset organization:
- Image and icon management
- Style and script organization
- PDF document handling
- Content compression rules

